gpc:10007760  rdf:type   gpc:Brick;
        rdfs:comment     "Includes any products that may be described/observed as a cement that has high flow characteristics and, in contrast to traditional concrete, does not require the addition of excessive amounts of water for placement. Self-leveling concrete is typically used to create a flat and smooth surface with a compressive strength similar to or higher than that of traditional concrete prior to installing interior floor coverings. Excludes any other type of mortar mixes, grouts, cement/mortar mixes, sealants, fillers or caulkers.&#160;&#160;"@en;
        rdfs:label       "Leveling Cement/Mortar"@en;
