gpc:50350000  rdf:type   gpc:Family;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to fresh plant leaves eaten as a vegetable. They are also called greens, vegetable greens, leafy greens or salad greens and potherbs. They may include tender petioles, the stalk that joins a leaf to a stem, and shoots which share nutrition and cooking methods with other leaf vegetables."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Leaf Vegetables - Unprepared/Unprocessed (Fresh)"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50000000 .

gpc:50350100  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to Chicory leaves, a somewhat woody, perennial herbaceous plant leaf which are cultivated for salad leaves. It is native to Europe, and in North America and Australia, where it has become naturalized."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Chicory Leaves"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350200  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to Head/Iceberg Lettuce of varieties (cultivars) grown from Lactuca sativa L. var. capitata L. to be supplied fresh."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Head Lettuce"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350300  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to loose or multi leaf lettuce grown from Lactuca sativa L. var. crispa L. to be supplied fresh."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Loose Leaf/Multileaf Salad Greens"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350400  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to single leaf greens of varieties (cultivars) grown from all botanical species to be supplied fresh."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Single Leaf Salad Greens"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350500  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This Class contains Spinach (Spinacia oleracea), an edible flowering plant in the family of Amaranthaceae. While native to central and south western Asia, it is commonly grown through out the world. It grows to a height of up to 30 cm long and 1-15 cm broad, with larger leaves at the base of the plant and small leaves higher on the flowering stem. Spinach has a high nutritional value and is extremely rich in antioxidants, especially when fresh, steamed, or quickly boiled. It is rich in vitamins."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Spinach (Fresh)"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350600  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:label       "Leaf Vegetables - Unprepared/Unprocessed Variety Packs"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

gpc:50350700  rdf:type   gpc:Class;
        rdfs:comment     "This standard applies to Stem Lettuce of varieties (cultivars) grown from&#160; Lactuca sativa&#160;var.&#160;asparagina,&#160;augustana, or&#160;angustata &#160;to be supplied fresh."@en;
        rdfs:label       "Stem Lettuce"@en;
        rdfs:subClassOf  gpc:50350000 .

